1
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:48,030
[When I Meet The Moon]

2
00:01:48,100 --> 00:01:50,990
[Episode 7]

3
00:02:01,350 --> 00:02:02,150
It finally succeeded!

4
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:02,850
-It succeeded!
-It succeeded!

5
00:02:02,850 --> 00:02:04,310
The experiment is over!

6
00:02:04,700 --> 00:02:05,790
Good job, Yun Li!

7
00:02:07,450 --> 00:02:08,810
The classic trial-and-error method

8
00:02:08,810 --> 00:02:09,710
and the adaptive control method

9
00:02:09,710 --> 00:02:11,090
have both been tried 3 times.

10
00:02:11,090 --> 00:02:12,910
The parameters should be optimal now.

11
00:02:12,910 --> 00:02:13,690
Good job, Yun Li.

12
00:02:13,690 --> 00:02:15,620
We can report to the professor now.

13
00:02:15,860 --> 00:02:16,860
We are all awesome.

14
00:02:16,860 --> 00:02:17,300
Yes.

15
00:02:17,300 --> 00:02:17,810
Good job, everyone.

16
00:02:17,810 --> 00:02:18,470
Good job.

17
00:02:21,980 --> 00:02:23,130
[Tang Lin]

18
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,340
Hello, Tangy.

19
00:02:27,560 --> 00:02:28,250
What are you doing?

20
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:29,300
Why didn't you reply to my messages?

21
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:30,910
I... I was doing an experiment.

22
00:02:30,910 --> 00:02:32,020
I didn't check my phone.

23
00:02:32,020 --> 00:02:33,820
Let's go out for dinner tonight.

24
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:35,960
Why the sudden treat?

25
00:02:36,060 --> 00:02:37,300
Did you win the lottery?

26
00:02:37,300 --> 00:02:38,310
I saw a restaurant online.

27
00:02:38,310 --> 00:02:39,690
They say it's really good.

28
00:02:39,690 --> 00:02:41,020
Let's go try it together.

29
00:02:41,020 --> 00:02:42,710
Okay, see you tonight.

30
00:02:42,710 --> 00:02:43,400
Okay.

31
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,500
Bye-bye.

32
00:03:00,410 --> 00:03:00,970
Hello?

33
00:03:01,430 --> 00:03:02,030
Shize,

34
00:03:02,690 --> 00:03:04,120
Grandma's birthday dinner is tonight.

35
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:05,150
Don't forget.

36
00:03:14,200 --> 00:03:16,960
-Happy birthday, Grandma!
-Happy birthday, Grandma!

37
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:17,750
Thank you!

38
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,150
Thank you. Let's clink glasses!

39
00:03:20,150 --> 00:03:20,800
Okay.

40
00:03:22,910 --> 00:03:23,690
Did Shize arrange

41
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:25,490
everything on this table today?

42
00:03:25,750 --> 00:03:27,090
He's so thoughtful.

43
00:03:27,310 --> 00:03:28,620
Shize arranged it.

44
00:03:28,860 --> 00:03:29,650
You see,

45
00:03:29,990 --> 00:03:30,650
only

46
00:03:30,670 --> 00:03:32,020
two professors like Uncle and Aunt

47
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:32,860
could raise

48
00:03:32,860 --> 00:03:34,410
such an excellent child.

49
00:03:35,690 --> 00:03:36,500
Shize,

50
00:03:36,860 --> 00:03:38,020
wish your mom a happy birthday

51
00:03:38,020 --> 00:03:39,350
and say something nice.

52
00:03:43,520 --> 00:03:44,310
Mom,

53
00:03:45,710 --> 00:03:46,640
happy birthday.

54
00:03:48,980 --> 00:03:51,910
You don't reply to messages
in the family group chat.

55
00:03:52,000 --> 00:03:54,710
So you finally decided to show up today?

56
00:03:56,690 --> 00:03:57,500
Exactly.

57
00:03:57,960 --> 00:03:59,560
If it weren't for your mom's birthday,

58
00:03:59,560 --> 00:04:01,360
it would be hard for us to see you.

59
00:04:07,060 --> 00:04:07,920
Here, Grandma.

60
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:08,960
Let me toast you.

61
00:04:09,310 --> 00:04:10,590
Happy birthday.

62
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:12,120
May you stay young forever.

63
00:04:12,120 --> 00:04:12,960
Happy birthday, Grandma!

64
00:04:12,960 --> 00:04:13,800
Happy birthday, Grandma!

65
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:14,910
Okay, thank you.

66
00:04:26,800 --> 00:04:28,560
The food here is so delicious.

67
00:04:29,190 --> 00:04:30,810
Xia is missing out.

68
00:04:31,060 --> 00:04:31,810
I sent her a message,

69
00:04:31,810 --> 00:04:33,340
but she hasn't replied yet.

70
00:04:36,450 --> 00:04:38,250
She hasn't replied to me either.

71
00:04:38,250 --> 00:04:39,450
She must be busy.

72
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:44,000
Lili,

73
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:44,750
look at Fu Zhengchu's

74
00:04:44,750 --> 00:04:45,680
post on Moments.

75
00:04:52,370 --> 00:04:54,980
Why are you suddenly

76
00:04:55,010 --> 00:04:56,670
so interested in Fu Zhengchu?

77
00:04:57,010 --> 00:04:58,159
I just saw it.

78
00:05:02,950 --> 00:05:03,950
"My grandma said

79
00:05:04,050 --> 00:05:05,310
birthdays should be celebrated in style."

80
00:05:05,310 --> 00:05:05,750
Today

81
00:05:05,750 --> 00:05:07,610
is Fu Shize's mother's birthday.

82
00:05:08,510 --> 00:05:10,170
Why don't you leave a comment?

83
00:05:11,810 --> 00:05:13,750
What should I comment?

84
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:16,420
"Happy birthday, Mother-in-Law."

85
00:05:16,660 --> 00:05:18,300
Don't talk nonsense.

86
00:05:19,510 --> 00:05:20,250
They are clearly

87
00:05:20,250 --> 00:05:21,660
a family of scholars.

88
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,360
This way,

89
00:05:22,360 --> 00:05:23,750
after you get married,

90
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:25,120
your parents-in-law will be reasonable.

91
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:26,250
Isn't that great?

92
00:05:26,710 --> 00:05:27,680
Think about it.

93
00:05:28,100 --> 00:05:29,130
Think about what?

94
00:05:29,130 --> 00:05:30,660
I can't win him over anyway.

95
00:05:33,230 --> 00:05:34,960
Did you give him the crepe roll?

96
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:36,040
Yes.

97
00:05:36,390 --> 00:05:37,600
Did he say anything?

98
00:05:38,390 --> 00:05:41,560
Does "thank you" count?

99
00:05:41,890 --> 00:05:42,880
Hell no.

100
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:49,560
They say it's easy
for a girl to chase a boy.

101
00:05:49,560 --> 00:05:51,500
Why is it so hard for me?

102
00:05:52,500 --> 00:05:53,159
Why don't you

103
00:05:53,159 --> 00:05:54,830
just give up now?

104
00:05:55,360 --> 00:05:56,600
Actually, Xia's uncle

105
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:57,950
isn't that great.

106
00:05:58,800 --> 00:06:01,300
He just has good looks

107
00:06:01,330 --> 00:06:02,300
and a good family background.

108
00:06:02,300 --> 00:06:02,600
But—

109
00:06:02,600 --> 00:06:04,250
He always has a stern face.

110
00:06:04,250 --> 00:06:05,560
And you don't dare to talk to him.

111
00:06:05,560 --> 00:06:06,250
You two look like

112
00:06:06,250 --> 00:06:07,650
you're performing mime.

113
00:06:07,740 --> 00:06:09,940
He's just naturally quiet.

114
00:06:11,330 --> 00:06:12,830
Is it possible

115
00:06:12,890 --> 00:06:14,560
that you're just attracted

116
00:06:14,560 --> 00:06:15,560
by his good looks?

117
00:06:19,690 --> 00:06:21,690
I could stare at

118
00:06:22,100 --> 00:06:23,500
Fu Shize's face forever.

119
00:06:24,100 --> 00:06:25,050
Yun Li.

120
00:06:25,360 --> 00:06:26,800
Can good looks feed you?

121
00:06:27,160 --> 00:06:29,490
You'll get tired of that face eventually.

122
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:31,040
Let me tell you.

123
00:06:31,190 --> 00:06:32,360
A man

124
00:06:32,360 --> 00:06:34,159
shouldn't just have good looks.

125
00:06:34,300 --> 00:06:35,930
The most important thing is a good temper.

126
00:06:35,930 --> 00:06:37,790
Otherwise, what if he abuses you?

127
00:06:37,950 --> 00:06:39,570
He's actually a nice guy.

128
00:06:40,300 --> 00:06:42,240
If he's so good,

129
00:06:42,300 --> 00:06:43,700
why don't you ask him out?

130
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:45,159
I...

131
00:06:46,890 --> 00:06:47,770
Never mind.

132
00:06:52,330 --> 00:06:54,500
That's such a pity.

133
00:06:55,060 --> 00:06:56,330
If that face

134
00:06:56,330 --> 00:06:58,540
is only for other women
to see from now on,

135
00:06:58,540 --> 00:06:59,300
the moon in your heart

136
00:06:59,300 --> 00:07:00,360
will be taken away.

137
00:07:02,540 --> 00:07:06,100
From now on, the bright moon
will shine on another woman,

138
00:07:06,950 --> 00:07:08,500
but it won't shine on you.

139
00:07:10,360 --> 00:07:11,160
That won't do.

140
00:07:14,630 --> 00:07:15,430
Zhengchu.

141
00:07:15,500 --> 00:07:16,890
What year are you in college?

142
00:07:16,890 --> 00:07:17,690
Sophomore.

143
00:07:18,100 --> 00:07:19,190
How are your studies?

144
00:07:19,190 --> 00:07:21,250
Are you planning to go to grad school?

145
00:07:21,500 --> 00:07:22,500
Probably.

146
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:23,600
What do you mean by "probably"?

147
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:24,930
You definitely should.

148
00:07:25,130 --> 00:07:26,790
Follow your uncle's example.

149
00:07:27,100 --> 00:07:28,690
How can I compare to my uncle?

150
00:07:28,690 --> 00:07:29,510
He's a top student,

151
00:07:29,510 --> 00:07:30,930
and he's already been
admitted to a PhD program.

152
00:07:30,930 --> 00:07:32,920
Just eat some radish.

153
00:07:34,870 --> 00:07:35,680
Shize,

154
00:07:36,370 --> 00:07:38,630
you've been slacking off for over a year.

155
00:07:38,810 --> 00:07:39,930
Isn't it time to go back to school

156
00:07:39,930 --> 00:07:41,130
and finish your PhD?

157
00:07:45,420 --> 00:07:46,950
I haven't thought about it.

158
00:07:47,270 --> 00:07:48,330
Listen to your mom.

159
00:07:48,570 --> 00:07:49,870
Hurry up and finish your PhD,

160
00:07:49,870 --> 00:07:51,430
so we can have peace of mind.

161
00:07:51,810 --> 00:07:52,680
After you graduate,

162
00:07:52,680 --> 00:07:53,510
whatever plans

163
00:07:53,510 --> 00:07:54,240
or ideas you have,

164
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:55,680
it won't be too late.

165
00:07:57,120 --> 00:07:57,920
Grandma,

166
00:07:57,980 --> 00:07:58,920
don't worry.

167
00:07:59,570 --> 00:08:00,680
Shize is with me now,

168
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:01,870
and he's doing great.

169
00:08:01,870 --> 00:08:03,040
With Shize joining us,

170
00:08:03,040 --> 00:08:03,980
EAW's

171
00:08:03,980 --> 00:08:04,530
VR technology

172
00:08:04,530 --> 00:08:06,190
has made a huge breakthrough.

173
00:08:07,180 --> 00:08:08,310
If a person can't even

174
00:08:08,310 --> 00:08:09,570
finish their studies,

175
00:08:09,770 --> 00:08:10,630
what kind of achievements can they make

176
00:08:10,630 --> 00:08:12,010
in scientific research?

177
00:08:12,010 --> 00:08:14,270
I think you guys are just messing around.

178
00:08:15,220 --> 00:08:17,130
My company is doing very well.

179
00:08:18,740 --> 00:08:19,810
Society is developing

180
00:08:19,810 --> 00:08:20,680
so fast now,

181
00:08:21,220 --> 00:08:23,350
and your peers are all moving forward.

182
00:08:24,240 --> 00:08:25,300
You're the only one

183
00:08:25,540 --> 00:08:27,200
still stuck in the same place,

184
00:08:27,390 --> 00:08:29,050
without any sense of urgency.

185
00:08:30,100 --> 00:08:31,000
I don't care.

186
00:08:32,340 --> 00:08:34,000
What kind of attitude is that?

187
00:08:34,630 --> 00:08:35,340
How did we

188
00:08:35,340 --> 00:08:36,740
raise you?

189
00:08:37,150 --> 00:08:38,280
When facing setbacks and difficulties,

190
00:08:38,280 --> 00:08:39,740
you must learn to be strong

191
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:41,289
and overcome your own weaknesses,

192
00:08:41,289 --> 00:08:42,500
instead of giving up on yourself

193
00:08:42,500 --> 00:08:44,169
and wallowing in degradation!

194
00:08:44,169 --> 00:08:44,940
After you reported

195
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:45,980
Professor Che back then,

196
00:08:45,980 --> 00:08:47,200
he was fired

197
00:08:47,240 --> 00:08:48,630
and punished.

198
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:50,480
What more do you want?

199
00:08:50,700 --> 00:08:52,830
What does it matter if he was punished?

200
00:08:54,440 --> 00:08:55,770
Can it change anything?

201
00:08:55,770 --> 00:08:56,630
Fu Shize!

202
00:09:02,940 --> 00:09:03,740
Aunt.

203
00:09:03,940 --> 00:09:04,740
Aunt.

204
00:09:05,030 --> 00:09:06,200
Calm down.

205
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:07,600
Shize,

206
00:09:08,240 --> 00:09:09,370
don't blame your parents

207
00:09:09,370 --> 00:09:10,570
for being so anxious.

208
00:09:10,940 --> 00:09:12,100
I also think there's absolutely

209
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:13,980
no need to torture yourself like this.

210
00:09:13,980 --> 00:09:14,630
That incident

211
00:09:14,630 --> 00:09:16,090
wasn't your fault anyway.

212
00:09:16,340 --> 00:09:18,080
Besides, it's been so long,

213
00:09:18,100 --> 00:09:19,760
and it won't change anything.

214
00:09:20,390 --> 00:09:21,740
We all know that

215
00:09:21,740 --> 00:09:22,890
you are very sad.

216
00:09:35,000 --> 00:09:35,600
What are you sending?

217
00:09:35,600 --> 00:09:36,390
Let me see.

218
00:09:43,370 --> 00:09:44,770
H-He's calling on video.

219
00:09:44,770 --> 00:09:46,310
Answer it quickly.

220
00:09:46,340 --> 00:09:47,120
What should I say?

221
00:09:47,120 --> 00:09:47,740
I...

222
00:09:48,080 --> 00:09:48,870
Just ask him

223
00:09:48,910 --> 00:09:49,580
when he's free

224
00:09:49,580 --> 00:09:50,380
to go on a date.

225
00:09:57,800 --> 00:09:58,890
Hello, Lili.

226
00:10:03,720 --> 00:10:05,370
Are you guys having a party?

227
00:10:05,410 --> 00:10:06,200
Yeah.

228
00:10:06,340 --> 00:10:07,740
We just finished dinner.

229
00:10:08,130 --> 00:10:09,220
Why is it you?

230
00:10:09,320 --> 00:10:10,320
Where's your uncle?

231
00:10:10,320 --> 00:10:11,120
Uncle.

232
00:10:13,080 --> 00:10:14,340
She's looking for you.

233
00:10:15,870 --> 00:10:17,520
Uncle, why are you ignoring her?

234
00:10:17,520 --> 00:10:18,830
Lili, I'm sorry.

235
00:10:19,030 --> 00:10:20,620
My uncle is a little bit...

236
00:10:20,840 --> 00:10:21,630
rude today.

237
00:10:22,270 --> 00:10:23,600
I haven't even seen her.

238
00:10:23,740 --> 00:10:24,800
How can I say hello?

239
00:10:29,740 --> 00:10:30,820
Long time no see.

240
00:10:33,510 --> 00:10:34,130
Hello.

241
00:10:36,030 --> 00:10:37,970
Yun Li, what are you talking about?

242
00:10:43,580 --> 00:10:45,100
Sang Yan opened a bar,

243
00:10:45,860 --> 00:10:46,790
called Overtime.

244
00:10:46,790 --> 00:10:47,890
Do you want to go check it out?

245
00:10:47,890 --> 00:10:48,750
I want to go too.

246
00:10:50,480 --> 00:10:51,290
Lili,

247
00:10:51,360 --> 00:10:52,150
we have something to do,

248
00:10:52,150 --> 00:10:53,450
so we'll talk to you later.

249
00:10:53,450 --> 00:10:55,180
Are you guys going to Overtime?

250
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:57,050
We happen to be going there too.

251
00:10:58,340 --> 00:10:59,530
I heard that place

252
00:10:59,530 --> 00:11:00,250
has really good business.

253
00:11:00,250 --> 00:11:01,440
How about we go first

254
00:11:01,440 --> 00:11:02,700
and save us some seats?

255
00:11:02,750 --> 00:11:03,360
Okay.

256
00:11:03,360 --> 00:11:04,420
See you later then.

257
00:11:05,740 --> 00:11:06,600
See you later.

258
00:11:08,600 --> 00:11:09,840
Nice move.

259
00:11:10,960 --> 00:11:11,790
Well done.

260
00:11:42,250 --> 00:11:43,000
Welcome.

261
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,340
Hello, welcome.

262
00:11:46,010 --> 00:11:48,240
Here's your umbrella. Thank you.

263
00:11:48,550 --> 00:11:49,030
Okay.

264
00:11:51,670 --> 00:11:52,740
This is...

265
00:11:53,570 --> 00:11:54,960
These are all to be destroyed.

266
00:11:54,960 --> 00:11:55,760
They're free.

267
00:11:57,670 --> 00:11:58,480
Um,

268
00:11:59,200 --> 00:12:00,130
I'm off work today.

269
00:12:00,130 --> 00:12:01,730
Do you want to walk together?

270
00:12:03,390 --> 00:12:04,340
Wait for me.

271
00:12:21,540 --> 00:12:23,360
[High School Must-Solve Problems]

272
00:12:30,120 --> 00:12:32,050
Are you also a high school sophomore?

273
00:12:32,050 --> 00:12:33,310
Yeah, how did you know?

274
00:12:34,250 --> 00:12:36,000
I just saw your workbook.

275
00:12:37,580 --> 00:12:38,630
What about you?

276
00:12:38,860 --> 00:12:40,060
I'm also a sophomore.

277
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:42,100
You're also a sophomore?

278
00:12:42,500 --> 00:12:44,050
Then... we are

279
00:12:44,050 --> 00:12:44,750
in the same school

280
00:12:44,750 --> 00:12:45,650
and the same grade.

281
00:12:45,650 --> 00:12:47,580
How come I haven't seen you before?

282
00:12:48,860 --> 00:12:51,220
Maybe I'm a bit introverted.

283
00:12:53,290 --> 00:12:54,650
I forgot to introduce myself.

284
00:12:54,650 --> 00:12:55,620
My name is Yun Ye.

285
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:56,510
Yun, meaning "cloud,"

286
00:12:56,510 --> 00:12:57,910
and Ye, meaning "field."

287
00:13:04,320 --> 00:13:05,650
My name is Yin Yunyi.

288
00:13:05,960 --> 00:13:06,910
I know your name.

289
00:13:09,720 --> 00:13:11,450
I saw your name badge last time.

290
00:13:14,320 --> 00:13:15,390
Our names

291
00:13:15,390 --> 00:13:16,700
are only one character apart.

292
00:13:16,700 --> 00:13:17,500
Yun Ye.

293
00:13:17,550 --> 00:13:18,360
Yunyi.

294
00:13:22,100 --> 00:13:23,250
How do you have time

295
00:13:23,250 --> 00:13:24,980
to work at a convenience store?

296
00:13:26,250 --> 00:13:27,500
It's not really a part-time job.

297
00:13:27,500 --> 00:13:30,430
I just help out
at my relative's place occasionally.

298
00:13:31,240 --> 00:13:33,570
My family is too strict with my allowance.

299
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:34,620
Same here.

300
00:13:36,160 --> 00:13:37,620
Is that why you always buy

301
00:13:37,620 --> 00:13:39,220
food that's about to expire?

302
00:13:42,410 --> 00:13:43,550
The allowance my family gives me

303
00:13:43,550 --> 00:13:44,750
is fixed.

304
00:13:44,890 --> 00:13:46,200
I have to save money

305
00:13:46,700 --> 00:13:47,510
to buy things

306
00:13:47,510 --> 00:13:48,790
that I like.

307
00:13:50,510 --> 00:13:52,480
Then you can be like me

308
00:13:52,620 --> 00:13:54,350
and earn some extra money here.

309
00:13:54,480 --> 00:13:55,630
I don't have time.

310
00:13:55,870 --> 00:13:57,330
I have to go to cram school.

311
00:13:58,050 --> 00:13:58,570
No wonder

312
00:13:58,570 --> 00:13:59,980
you always come so late.

313
00:14:00,820 --> 00:14:02,420
What classes are you taking?

314
00:14:02,740 --> 00:14:03,530
English.

315
00:14:04,830 --> 00:14:07,030
I'm going to study abroad in the future.

316
00:14:39,010 --> 00:14:40,670
This bar looks pretty good.

317
00:14:42,010 --> 00:14:42,820
Xia.

318
00:14:43,240 --> 00:14:44,170
Tangy, over here.

319
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:44,910
Xia.

320
00:14:47,170 --> 00:14:48,840
Lili, you look so pretty today.

321
00:14:48,840 --> 00:14:49,370
Of course.

322
00:14:49,370 --> 00:14:51,170
Tangy put together a look for me.

323
00:14:51,220 --> 00:14:52,030
Have a seat.

324
00:14:58,770 --> 00:14:59,580
Lili.

325
00:14:59,580 --> 00:15:00,980
You look so pretty today,

326
00:15:00,980 --> 00:15:02,580
quite different from usual.

327
00:15:02,910 --> 00:15:03,720
Thank you.

328
00:15:04,910 --> 00:15:06,370
Are you here

329
00:15:06,370 --> 00:15:07,530
to find a boyfriend?

330
00:15:07,530 --> 00:15:09,390
You really don't know how to talk.

331
00:15:10,770 --> 00:15:11,740
Can't you learn from Lili

332
00:15:11,740 --> 00:15:12,670
and be a bit gentler?

333
00:15:12,670 --> 00:15:13,080
Coming here,

334
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:14,630
you didn't even change your clothes.

335
00:15:14,630 --> 00:15:16,090
None of your business.

336
00:15:18,280 --> 00:15:19,080
It's fine.

337
00:15:20,720 --> 00:15:22,080
Why is it just the two of you?

338
00:15:22,080 --> 00:15:23,280
Where are the others?

339
00:15:24,320 --> 00:15:25,510
Qingsong went to find the bar owner

340
00:15:25,510 --> 00:15:26,370
to chat.

341
00:15:27,080 --> 00:15:27,910
This place

342
00:15:27,910 --> 00:15:29,770
is also opened by Mr. Xu's friend?

343
00:15:31,270 --> 00:15:32,170
When Fu Zhengchu was a kid,

344
00:15:32,170 --> 00:15:33,790
he even chased after the owner's sister.

345
00:15:33,790 --> 00:15:34,480
Congsheng.

346
00:15:34,530 --> 00:15:35,390
That was so many years ago.

347
00:15:35,390 --> 00:15:35,890
It's fine.

348
00:15:35,890 --> 00:15:36,690
Stop talking.

349
00:15:37,630 --> 00:15:38,840
Really?

350
00:15:39,200 --> 00:15:40,130
What kind of girl is she?

351
00:15:40,130 --> 00:15:40,940
Is she pretty?

352
00:15:41,630 --> 00:15:42,720
Anyway, prettier than you

353
00:15:42,720 --> 00:15:43,920
and gentler than you.

354
00:15:49,260 --> 00:15:49,830
Fu...

355
00:15:50,990 --> 00:15:53,310
Did Fu Shize also go to say hi?

356
00:15:53,580 --> 00:15:55,440
Uncle is sitting at the bar.

357
00:16:04,870 --> 00:16:06,080
Around Fu Shize,

358
00:16:06,080 --> 00:16:08,140
has there never been any other woman?

359
00:16:08,510 --> 00:16:09,410
How is that possible?

360
00:16:09,410 --> 00:16:10,220
With his looks,

361
00:16:10,220 --> 00:16:11,720
even if he does nothing,

362
00:16:11,720 --> 00:16:13,370
many women would lean on him.

363
00:16:13,510 --> 00:16:14,150
Then why hasn't he

364
00:16:14,150 --> 00:16:16,010
been in a relationship even once?

365
00:16:16,370 --> 00:16:17,220
He is so aloof

366
00:16:17,220 --> 00:16:18,350
and ignores people.

367
00:16:22,750 --> 00:16:24,220
Then if a girl

368
00:16:24,220 --> 00:16:25,350
wants to pursue him,

369
00:16:25,410 --> 00:16:26,270
do you think

370
00:16:26,870 --> 00:16:28,130
it's highly possible?

371
00:16:29,770 --> 00:16:31,390
I think

372
00:16:32,270 --> 00:16:34,770
the success rate is zero.

373
00:16:35,510 --> 00:16:36,270
He is so aloof

374
00:16:36,270 --> 00:16:36,980
and ignores people.

375
00:16:36,980 --> 00:16:38,480
Who would go to that trouble?

376
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:39,530
I think so too.

377
00:16:41,840 --> 00:16:42,840
Then what if someone

378
00:16:42,840 --> 00:16:44,700
insists on going to that trouble?

379
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,550
No one would be that stupid, right?

380
00:16:53,080 --> 00:16:54,010
Are you alone?

381
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:03,530
Um, I'll go order a drink.

382
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:05,420
Okay.

383
00:17:09,290 --> 00:17:10,849
Sis, wait a minute.

384
00:17:14,700 --> 00:17:15,500
Little girl,

385
00:17:15,790 --> 00:17:16,660
when it comes to hitting on someone,

386
00:17:16,660 --> 00:17:18,089
it's first come, first served. Understand?

387
00:17:18,089 --> 00:17:18,849
Besides,

388
00:17:18,849 --> 00:17:20,310
who are you calling "Sis"?

389
00:17:20,940 --> 00:17:22,400
I'm not here to hit on him.

390
00:17:24,530 --> 00:17:25,589
I'm his friend.

391
00:17:26,349 --> 00:17:27,440
Besides, in our circle,

392
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:28,900
many people are students.

393
00:17:29,140 --> 00:17:30,350
Don't force my friend

394
00:17:30,350 --> 00:17:31,400
to drink with you.

395
00:17:31,850 --> 00:17:32,650
Otherwise, I'll call

396
00:17:32,650 --> 00:17:33,660
the counselor.

397
00:17:34,940 --> 00:17:35,790
Counselor?

398
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:37,640
I never thought I'd hear that word

399
00:17:37,640 --> 00:17:38,900
in a bar in my life.

400
00:17:40,660 --> 00:17:43,160
Why are kids coming to bars?

401
00:17:53,290 --> 00:17:53,960
Yun Lili.

402
00:17:56,050 --> 00:17:56,530
Sit.

403
00:18:10,500 --> 00:18:12,140
Why did you call me

404
00:18:12,140 --> 00:18:13,380
Yun Lili?

405
00:18:13,800 --> 00:18:15,610
Did you remember my name wrong?

406
00:18:24,570 --> 00:18:25,090
Mm.

407
00:18:28,700 --> 00:18:29,480
That's fine.

408
00:18:29,840 --> 00:18:31,680
You can call me whatever you want.

409
00:18:31,680 --> 00:18:32,940
It sounds pretty good.

410
00:18:36,510 --> 00:18:37,910
What do you want to drink?

411
00:18:43,440 --> 00:18:44,700
What are you drinking?

412
00:18:45,070 --> 00:18:45,880
Whiskey.

413
00:18:46,330 --> 00:18:47,680
I'll have a whiskey too.

414
00:18:48,180 --> 00:18:48,610
Okay.

415
00:18:48,610 --> 00:18:49,810
Make her a soft drink.

416
00:18:49,940 --> 00:18:50,460
Okay.

417
00:18:58,770 --> 00:19:01,110
They all say people come to bars

418
00:19:01,110 --> 00:19:03,770
to find a partner.

419
00:19:04,290 --> 00:19:05,820
Are you looking for one too?

420
00:19:11,310 --> 00:19:12,630
Do you want to find a partner?

421
00:19:12,630 --> 00:19:13,500
I don't.

422
00:19:15,570 --> 00:19:18,270
You can't answer a question
with a question.

423
00:19:18,960 --> 00:19:19,750
Why?

424
00:19:21,310 --> 00:19:22,220
Because if you ask,

425
00:19:22,220 --> 00:19:24,570
I'll seriously think about how to answer.

426
00:19:24,770 --> 00:19:25,660
And if I answer,

427
00:19:25,660 --> 00:19:26,510
this conversation

428
00:19:26,510 --> 00:19:28,160
won't be able to continue.

429
00:19:34,270 --> 00:19:36,400
You haven't answered my question yet.

430
00:19:41,850 --> 00:19:42,660
I'm not.

431
00:19:47,980 --> 00:19:48,770
Thank you.

432
00:19:59,290 --> 00:20:00,890
Maybe you should drink less?

433
00:20:02,220 --> 00:20:03,010
It's fine.

434
00:20:08,090 --> 00:20:09,090
You drink mine.

435
00:20:09,460 --> 00:20:11,190
I'll drink with you for a while.

436
00:20:14,640 --> 00:20:15,270
It burns.

437
00:20:19,110 --> 00:20:19,720
No need.

438
00:20:19,720 --> 00:20:20,960
I'll just drink this.

439
00:20:28,140 --> 00:20:28,980
Why are you two sitting here

440
00:20:28,980 --> 00:20:29,640
chatting?

441
00:20:29,640 --> 00:20:30,070
Come play games

442
00:20:30,070 --> 00:20:30,750
with us.

443
00:20:31,030 --> 00:20:31,560
Let's go.

444
00:20:33,010 --> 00:20:33,570
Let's go.

445
00:20:34,160 --> 00:20:34,740
Come on.

446
00:20:35,120 --> 00:20:35,650
Let's go.

447
00:20:36,530 --> 00:20:37,390
Let's go, Lili.

448
00:20:42,660 --> 00:20:43,790
Uncle, hurry up too.

449
00:20:44,090 --> 00:20:44,510
Hurry.

450
00:20:53,140 --> 00:20:53,510
Perfect.

451
00:20:53,510 --> 00:20:54,380
Lili, you sit here.

452
00:20:54,380 --> 00:20:55,370
I'll teach you how to play Liar's Dice.

453
00:20:55,370 --> 00:20:56,570
The rules are very simple.

454
00:20:56,570 --> 00:20:57,770
I can teach her that too.

455
00:20:57,770 --> 00:21:00,300
Why do you have to get
involved in everything?

456
00:21:06,090 --> 00:21:06,690
Move over.

457
00:21:07,200 --> 00:21:07,590
Okay.

458
00:21:10,740 --> 00:21:11,740
Move further out.

459
00:21:22,590 --> 00:21:23,090
Uncle,

460
00:21:23,110 --> 00:21:24,500
don't steal my seat.

461
00:21:24,920 --> 00:21:26,380
I don't want to sit next to Tang Lin.

462
00:21:26,380 --> 00:21:27,240
Are you scared?

463
00:21:27,510 --> 00:21:29,330
If you beg for mercy now,

464
00:21:29,480 --> 00:21:31,740
I might go easy on you.

465
00:21:33,770 --> 00:21:34,940
Who's scared of who?

466
00:21:37,140 --> 00:21:38,380
Can't you be gentle

467
00:21:38,380 --> 00:21:39,220
like Lili?

468
00:21:41,550 --> 00:21:41,940
Lili,

469
00:21:41,940 --> 00:21:42,830
maybe you should sit here.

470
00:21:42,830 --> 00:21:44,560
I feel like my life is in danger.

471
00:21:47,420 --> 00:21:48,220
Let's start.

472
00:21:49,070 --> 00:21:49,510
Oh, right.

473
00:21:49,510 --> 00:21:50,770
Lili doesn't know the rules yet.

474
00:21:50,770 --> 00:21:51,530
So,

475
00:21:51,680 --> 00:21:52,510
we'll start with me,

476
00:21:52,510 --> 00:21:54,030
then Uncle,

477
00:21:54,030 --> 00:21:54,530
Lili,

478
00:21:54,530 --> 00:21:55,330
and so on.

479
00:21:55,330 --> 00:21:55,680
Lili,

480
00:21:55,680 --> 00:21:57,140
if you think the person before you

481
00:21:57,140 --> 00:21:57,720
is bluffing,

482
00:21:57,720 --> 00:21:58,640
you call them out.

483
00:21:58,640 --> 00:21:59,880
If you guess right,

484
00:21:59,880 --> 00:22:00,530
they drink.

485
00:22:00,530 --> 00:22:01,810
If you guess wrong,

486
00:22:01,830 --> 00:22:02,740
you drink.

487
00:22:02,740 --> 00:22:04,220
Got it?

488
00:22:05,310 --> 00:22:06,110
I don't...

489
00:22:06,110 --> 00:22:06,710
It's fine.

490
00:22:07,270 --> 00:22:09,070
You'll get it after a few rounds.

491
00:22:10,740 --> 00:22:12,270
Then let's start with me.

492
00:22:21,440 --> 00:22:22,110
Five ones.

493
00:22:22,980 --> 00:22:23,500
Call.

494
00:22:25,770 --> 00:22:26,680
What are you doing, Uncle?

495
00:22:26,680 --> 00:22:28,480
Who would call on the first turn?

496
00:22:29,740 --> 00:22:30,220
None.

497
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,170
I don't have any.

498
00:22:31,310 --> 00:22:32,030
One.

499
00:22:32,030 --> 00:22:32,740
One.

500
00:22:33,310 --> 00:22:34,570
You lost, Fu Zhengchu.

501
00:22:34,830 --> 00:22:36,030
Five people, and we can't even

502
00:22:36,030 --> 00:22:37,070
scrape together 5 ones?

503
00:22:37,070 --> 00:22:37,880
Drink up.

504
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:40,830
This... My...

505
00:22:42,980 --> 00:22:43,980
My drink.

506
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:46,420
We're all friends here.

507
00:22:46,420 --> 00:22:47,550
Don't be a stranger.

508
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:49,440
Off to a bad start.

509
00:22:49,440 --> 00:22:50,970
Let's start with you again.

510
00:22:53,160 --> 00:22:55,420
I don't believe I can lose this round too.

511
00:22:59,530 --> 00:23:00,330
Ten sixes.

512
00:23:00,530 --> 00:23:02,000
Six... Ten...

513
00:23:03,980 --> 00:23:04,770
Call.

514
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,830
What are you doing, Uncle?

515
00:23:09,830 --> 00:23:11,400
Fu Zhengchu lost again.

516
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,590
Hurry up and drink.

517
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:15,270
Mine.

518
00:23:15,370 --> 00:23:16,140
Grabbed the wrong one.

519
00:23:16,140 --> 00:23:18,140
I'm getting desperate from losing.

520
00:23:20,200 --> 00:23:21,000
Come on!

521
00:23:21,530 --> 00:23:23,790
I don't believe I can lose this round too.

522
00:23:24,740 --> 00:23:25,530
Ten sixes!

523
00:23:25,530 --> 00:23:26,270
Call.

524
00:23:28,570 --> 00:23:29,380
Drink.

525
00:23:31,160 --> 00:23:31,940
Call.

526
00:23:32,510 --> 00:23:33,270
Call.

527
00:23:35,050 --> 00:23:36,250
Why do you keep losing?

528
00:23:36,250 --> 00:23:38,180
Can you do this or not, Fu Zhengchu?

529
00:23:40,790 --> 00:23:41,590
Well...

530
00:23:43,590 --> 00:23:44,400
Continue.

531
00:23:46,290 --> 00:23:47,090
Old Auntie.

532
00:23:49,420 --> 00:23:50,960
Tangy, you're so nice.

533
00:23:52,660 --> 00:23:53,660
Don't call me that.

534
00:23:53,660 --> 00:23:54,920
It's disgusting.

535
00:23:55,660 --> 00:23:56,810
You guys are already playing.

536
00:23:56,810 --> 00:23:58,010
What are you playing?

537
00:23:58,250 --> 00:23:59,220
Playing Liar's Dice.

538
00:23:59,220 --> 00:24:00,680
Qingsong, want to join us?

539
00:24:00,790 --> 00:24:01,310
Come on.

540
00:24:01,310 --> 00:24:02,290
I'm the best at this.

541
00:24:02,290 --> 00:24:03,000
Hurry up.

542
00:24:04,010 --> 00:24:06,310
Can we start with me next round?

543
00:24:07,230 --> 00:24:08,860
I kind of want to try.

544
00:24:09,400 --> 00:24:10,200
Good idea.

545
00:24:10,220 --> 00:24:11,250
Since Qingsong is here,

546
00:24:11,250 --> 00:24:12,610
let's start with Lili.

547
00:24:12,610 --> 00:24:13,550
We'll go in the opposite direction.

548
00:24:13,550 --> 00:24:15,660
I don't believe
I can still lose like this!

549
00:24:15,660 --> 00:24:16,550
Come on.

550
00:24:18,880 --> 00:24:19,400
Come on.

551
00:24:27,400 --> 00:24:28,940
Twelve sixes.

552
00:24:30,050 --> 00:24:30,680
Lili,

553
00:24:30,680 --> 00:24:32,090
do you want to change it?

554
00:24:32,090 --> 00:24:32,900
Twelve sixes.

555
00:24:32,990 --> 00:24:35,030
Uncle will definitely call your bluff.

556
00:24:35,030 --> 00:24:35,680
It's...

557
00:24:35,680 --> 00:24:36,480
Thirteen.

558
00:24:38,500 --> 00:24:39,290
Uncle.

559
00:24:40,000 --> 00:24:40,790
Thirteen sixes?

560
00:24:40,790 --> 00:24:41,720
Are you serious?

561
00:24:41,900 --> 00:24:42,700
Your turn.

562
00:24:44,030 --> 00:24:45,070
Then I won't hold back.

563
00:24:45,070 --> 00:24:45,770
Call!

564
00:24:47,400 --> 00:24:49,090
Fu Zhengchu, you lost.

565
00:24:49,440 --> 00:24:51,030
There really are 13 sixes.

566
00:24:52,500 --> 00:24:53,290
Wait!

567
00:24:53,400 --> 00:24:54,500
Something's wrong.

568
00:24:54,500 --> 00:24:55,290
Uncle,

569
00:24:55,640 --> 00:24:56,330
are you targeting me

570
00:24:56,330 --> 00:24:57,640
tonight?

571
00:25:01,070 --> 00:25:03,500
Do you have feelings for Lili?

572
00:25:07,980 --> 00:25:08,780
You guys play.

573
00:25:10,750 --> 00:25:12,150
Come on, let's continue.

574
00:25:33,240 --> 00:25:34,200
Cute.

575
00:25:39,250 --> 00:25:41,420
Why isn't he back yet?

576
00:25:46,460 --> 00:25:47,250
Cute.

577
00:25:48,380 --> 00:25:49,720
The cute type.

578
00:25:49,880 --> 00:25:50,680
You lost again.

579
00:25:50,680 --> 00:25:51,160
Tangy,

580
00:25:51,360 --> 00:25:52,890
I'm going to the restroom.

581
00:25:54,350 --> 00:25:55,380
You can't beat me.

582
00:26:05,860 --> 00:26:06,660
Fu Shize.

583
00:26:14,050 --> 00:26:14,850
Yun Lili.

584
00:26:19,310 --> 00:26:20,840
You've been here all along?

585
00:26:22,350 --> 00:26:22,850
Mm.

586
00:26:23,180 --> 00:26:24,960
Then why didn't I see you?

587
00:26:25,510 --> 00:26:26,840
Were you looking for me?

588
00:26:27,400 --> 00:26:27,900
Yeah.

589
00:26:28,600 --> 00:26:29,800
I was looking for you.

590
00:26:30,680 --> 00:26:32,510
I-I'm here to take you back.

591
00:26:34,810 --> 00:26:35,670
Where are they?

592
00:26:36,480 --> 00:26:39,070
They drank a bit too much.

593
00:26:39,270 --> 00:26:40,640
They can barely walk.

594
00:26:44,920 --> 00:26:45,720
Let's go back.

595
00:26:46,220 --> 00:26:46,720
Yeah.

596
00:27:14,510 --> 00:27:16,040
Do you want some sweet soup?

597
00:27:18,070 --> 00:27:19,660
When I'm in a bad mood,

598
00:27:19,660 --> 00:27:22,720
